// The file gate is a unit's FIRST line — before `import { … };`, which is before `export { … };`.
//
// One position, not several, because the gate decides whether the file exists at all for this build:
// anything written above it would be text the compiler had to make sense of before knowing whether the
// file was even in the compilation. The grammar puts it at the head of `compilation_unit` and nowhere
// else, so this is a parse error.
import { std::io };
file @compileFor(DEBUG);

fn int32 main() { return 0; }
